{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774144505,"nonce":"gYB3WnNq14KZiDPhMR5TM8u3lDY=","title":"Convention: agents should fix bugs immediately without asking for permission","message":"When the user reports a bug or a fix is identified, agents should immediately proceed to fix it — no \"should I fix this?\" or \"want me to fix it?\" The auth request mechanism already provides the user control point (they authenticate the merge). Asking before fixing wastes a round-trip.\n\nThis should be added to the global CLAUDE.md under Proactive Behaviors or Hard Constraints.\n\nProposed wording:\n\"When a bug is identified or the user reports broken behavior, fix it immediately. Do not ask whether to fix it — the auth request workflow provides the approval gate. The only exception is when a fix would require a large architectural change that should be discussed first.\"","files":null}]}